  "Number": 9,
  "Question": "What is the value of the product of the \\(9\\) factors below?\n\n\\[ \\begin{aligned} &\\left(1 - \\tfrac12\\right)\\left(1 - \\tfrac13\\right)\\left(1 - \\tfrac14\\right) \\cdots \\\\ &\\quad {}\\cdot \\left(1 - \\tfrac{1}{10}\\right) \\end{aligned} \\]",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\dfrac{1}{10}\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\dfrac{1}{9}\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\dfrac{10}{11}\\)",
    "E": "\\(\\dfrac{11}{2}\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "Subtracting each unit fraction from \\(1\\) gives a numerator one less than its denominator. For example, \\(1-\\frac13=\\frac23\\). Thus the nine factors become\n\\[\n\\frac12\\cdot\\frac23\\cdot\\frac34\\cdots\\frac9{10}\n=\\frac{1\\cdot2\\cdots9}{2\\cdot3\\cdots10}.\n\\]\nEvery integer from \\(2\\) through \\(9\\) appears once in both the numerator and denominator. Canceling these nonzero factors leaves \\(\\frac1{10}\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{A}\\).",
